Sam 
Thanks for the summary — this is exactly the right level of ask. Im attaching a one-page cutover checklist (BrightBank_cutover_checklist.xlsx) and a sample SDK bundle (redwood-sdk-samples-v2.zip) with minimal examples for Java/Python/Node. High-level plan below; Ill put the full runbook in the shared Drive link and create a short Jira for pre-cutover tasks.

Cutover highlights (short):
- Auth: Use service keys scoped to the staging gateway first; rotate before prod. We recommend 15m JWT expiry for short-lived tokens; rotate via CI secrets manager.
- Endpoint mapping: 1:1 mapping between legacy endpoints and Redwood routes. Start with read-only routes to validate responses.
- Traffic shaping: Canary 5% -> 25% -> 100% over separate windows. If latency increases > 50ms P95 or error rate > 1% revert to old endpoint.
- Rate limits: Default tier is 60 r/s per IP. For BrightBank we suggest a 600 r/s burst quota on Dedicated tier; we will provision during cutover.
- Retries/timeouts: Keep client timeouts slightly above server request timeout (client timeout = 10s, server SLO 8s). Retries: 3 attempts max with jittered exponential backoff (base=250ms, factor=2, max=4s). Avoid retrying non-idempotent POSTs without idempotency keys.

Quick Java retry snippet (from the sample bundle):

// Java (pseudocode)
HttpClient client = HttpClient.newBuilder().connectTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3)).build();
int attempts = 0;
long delay = 250;
while (attempts < 3) {
  try {
    HttpRequest req = HttpRequest.newBuilder().uri(URI.create("https://gateway.redwood.inference/api/v1/generate")).header("Authorization", "Bearer " + token).timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(10)).POST(BodyPublishers.ofString(payload)).build();
    HttpResponse<String> resp = client.send(req, BodyHandlers.ofString());
    if (resp.statusCode() == 200) { return resp.body(); }
    if (resp.statusCode() >= 500) { throw new IOException("server"); }
    // for 4xx, do not retry except 429
    if (resp.statusCode() == 429) { throw new IOException("rate_limited"); }
  } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
    attempts++;
    if (attempts >= 3) throw e;
    Thread.sleep(delay + ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextLong(0, 200));
    delay = Math.min(4000, delay * 2);
  }
}

Ill book a short 30-min run-through for Thursday to walk the team through the checklist and the sample code. Monica will own follow-ups on quotas and provisioning.

